{{! How the heat (how often each place was visited) is drawn, as JSON (its drawing, activities-map-heat.js, reads it): a smooth glow
    (Leaflet.heat), from `low` (a place visited once) through to `high` (the busiest), on a log scale; `min_opacity` is how
    faint the faintest heat is, `radius_cells` how far each cell's heat spreads, in cells (so the glow looks the same at every
    zoom; zoomed in so far that it would be more than 60 pixels, what Leaflet.heat can draw, the heat is not drawn: the
    routes say more there).  Each size of cell (`level`: 0 is about 100 m, 3 about 870 m, 6 about 7 km) is used from the zoom `min_zoom` (the
    finest that is allowed, else the coarsest). }}
{
  "low": "#ffd43b", "high": "{{{red}}}", "min_opacity": 0.3, "radius_cells": 1.5,
  "levels": [ { "level": 0, "min_zoom": 14 }, { "level": 3, "min_zoom": 11 }, { "level": 6, "min_zoom": 0 } ]
}
